  "problem": "The vector-valued function $f(\\theta ,ϕ),$ given by \n\n$$\nf(\\theta ,ϕ)=⟨3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\text{_______},3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ\\,⟩\n$$\n\nparametrizes the hyperboloid of one sheet defined in Cartesian coordinates as ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}=9.$ By expressing the equation of the hyperboloid in cylindrical polar coordinates, determine the second component of $f.$\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that the hyperbola ${r}^{2}-{z}^{2}={k}^{2}$ can be parametrized as $⟨r,z⟩=⟨k\\operatorname{cosh}⁡ϕ,k\\operatorname{sinh}⁡ϕ⟩$* for $ϕ\\in R.$",
